Why it is here
--------------
NEXT-STEPS.md §2.1 (`ask`) runs a whole declaration through a transformer
instead of adding up per-token vectors from a static table. That needs an
inference runtime inside the binary. `runs/ASK/T2-inference-runtime.json`
settled the choice with a working prototype rather than an assessment:
minimum cosine 0.999980 against sentence-transformers fp32 over 45 texts,
last-token pooling honoured from the GGUF's own metadata, a clean C11
`-Wall -Wextra -Werror` compile against a C-callable header, and a fully
static 7.7 MB binary. No alternative was needed and none is proposed.

The model weights are NOT here. They are fetched on first use of this lane
(`hyponoia fetch-model`), pinned by revision and verified against a SHA-256
compiled into the binary — see `src/cli/model_fetch.h` and
`runs/ASK/T7-model-fetch.json`. Q8_0 is 639 MB; embedding that in an artifact
every user of the other fifteen tools downloads was rejected on those grounds.

What was taken
--------------
A subset, not the repository:

  ggml/include/               ggml's public headers
  ggml/src/*.c,*.cpp,*.h      ggml-base and the backend registry
  ggml/src/ggml-cpu/          the CPU backend (minus spacemit/, see below)
  ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/       ggml-vulkan.cpp and the GLSL shader sources
  src/, include/llama*.h      the llama library

Excluded: tools/, examples/, tests/, common/, the bundled third-party vendor/
tree (minja, cpp-httplib), every non-CPU/non-Vulkan backend (CUDA, HIP, SYCL,
Metal, OpenCL, RPC, WebGPU, …), the Python conversion scripts, and the CMake
build. `ggml-cpu/spacemit/` is excluded specifically: it is a RISC-V TCM helper
this build never compiles, and it is the only file in the set that calls
`dlopen()`.

The ~200 MB of C++ that `vulkan-shaders-gen` emits from the `.comp` shaders is
a BUILD artifact under `build/c/vulkan-shaders/` and is deliberately not
committed. What supply-chain integrity needs is the GLSL it is generated from,
and that is here and checksummed.

Local modifications
-------------------
Two, twelve lines in total, both security-motivated and both described in full
in HYPONOIA-PATCHES.md:

  1. ggml/src/ggml-backend-dl.cpp — the POSIX `dlopen`/`dlsym` backend loader
     returns nullptr. Dead code in a static build; keeping it would put
     `dlopen` in a binary that has none today and break `-static`.
  2. ggml/src/ggml.c — `ggml_print_backtrace()` no longer forks and execs
     `gdb` against its own pid on abort. It prints a symbol backtrace instead.

Both are re-applied by `scripts/vendor-llama-cpp.sh`, which refuses rather than
silently skipping if upstream's code moves out from under them.

Reproducing this directory
--------------------------
    git clone https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
    git -C llama.cpp checkout 74ce15741b420b8d6f12e720398458b576c51c2c
    scripts/vendor-llama-cpp.sh llama.cpp
    scripts/security-vendored.sh
